$ akb workflow schedule coding --on builder
akb: `builder` does not declare `akb.hook: schedule`, so it cannot run on a cadence
(exit 1)

$ akb workflow schedule coding --on release-notes
akb: this board has no `release-notes` agent
(exit 1)

$ akb workflow schedule coding --cadence 1d
akb: --cadence says how often one agent runs, so name it: --on <agent> --cadence 1d
(exit 1)

$ akb workflow schedule coding --extra "Keep it short."
akb: --extra says what one agent is asked for here, so name it: --on <agent> --extra "…"
(exit 1)

$ akb workflow schedule coding --on changelog-keeper --cadence weekly
akb: "weekly" isn't a cadence — use <N>m (minutes), <N>h (hours), <N>d (days), or <N>d at HH:MM (whole days, at that time of day) — e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d at 09:30
(exit 1)

$ akb workflow schedule docs
akb: no workflow called "docs" on this board. It has: coding, hyperframes-video, slide-deck, carousel-post, blog-post.
(exit 1)

$ akb raw list --archived --since last-run
akb raw: --since last-run only works inside a scheduled agent's run. Elsewhere, write the time as "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM".
(exit 1)

